    "The x87 nonfaulting recurring CFG path has 222 instructions as-is/move,217 omit,207 future-bias. The15-instruction future reduction is exactly15 fewer MOVs; the unchanged61 loads/7stores include40 stack loads/7stack stores. This supports a changed register-shuffle realization, while the isolated timing does not establish a speedup.",
    "No timer data is produced by this audit. Prior symmetric same-Core counterfactual timing did not show improvement for omit/move/future versus as-is; static instruction/frame differences cannot establish an optimization or explain the historical whole-Core timing gap.",
    "No production code rewrite or IR-allocation-trace escalation is justified by this particular hypothesis: recurring original-B-slot traffic is absent."
